## 5. Frontend UI/UX Guide

The signatory screen lives inside the deposit account view (see [DepositAccount.md](DepositAccount.md) §6.3), tab **Signatories**.

| Item | Value |
|------|-------|
| Entry | Deposits → Deposit Accounts → View account → **Signatories** tab (deep link `/deposits/accounts/{account_id}?tab=signatories`) |
| APIs | `GET /api/DepositSignatoryList`, `POST /api/DepositSignatoryAdd`, `POST /api/DepositSignatoryEdit`, `POST /api/DepositSignatoryStatus` |
| Lookups | Group account: `GET /api/MemberGroupList?group_id={cust_id_primary}&is_active=1`. Individual: the account holders; for Authorised Signatory mode `GET /api/MemberList?status_cd=1&keyword=…` |

- Card per signatory: photo (`photo_file_nm`, else `member_photo_path`), name, ref code, mobile, `signatory_role` chip, specimen signature thumbnail (`sign_file_nm`, else `member_signature_path`). Actions ✏ Edit (files) and ⏻ Deactivate.
- **Add signatory** drawer: member select (filtered as in *Lookups*, excluding active signatories), signature / photo upload fields that store the uploaded file name. "+ Another signatory" adds a block. On `Signatory N: …` highlight block N (nothing was saved).
- Group accounts: suggest President, Secretary and Treasurer first.
- When `op_mode_cd = 5` and there is no active signatory, show an amber banner on the account: *Authorised Signatory account has no signatory yet.*
- Inactive rows under **Show inactive**, muted, with **Activate**. Hide all actions when the account is closed.

